&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director or Director, Laboratory Operations and Facilities is responsible for a lab and a building that run smoothly day-to-day and for the systems and processes that allow both to scale as Kymera grows.&amp;nbsp; This person works closely with the Executive Director, Facilities on the strategy for both functions, aligns on the annual goals, then leads execution.&amp;nbsp; This is an on-site, hands-on leadership role that partners with Research, EHS, IT, Finance, People + Culture, and Strategic Sourcing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with the Executive Director, Facilities on the annual goals that deliver the operations strategy, then own the plans, priorities, and operating budget to meet them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team spanning both functions; set clear expectations, plan capacity, delegate real ownership, and build coverage so no part of the operation depends on one person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary operations partner to Research leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the metrics, reporting, and service standards that show how both functions are performing, and use them to drive improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication with the research organization on lab changes, planned downtime, and new processes, and run a regular feedback loop with scientists that drives service improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own lab space planning: bench and equipment allocation, occupancy and capacity tracking, space taxonomy, and scenario modeling against the hiring plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the lab operations lead on lab build-outs, moves, and reconfigurations, providing requirements, equipment placement, and commissioning input.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the lab asset management and preventative-maintenance program, including equipment lifecycle, criticality, calibration, service contracts, and asset records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own cold-storage strategy and environmental monitoring; ensure alarm response has staffed 24/7 coverage, a written escalation tree, and no single point of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee consumables and lab inventory, including vendor-managed inventory, burn-rate reporting, and stockout prevention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee lab sample and shipping logistics, including hazardous-materials and cold-chain shipping (DOT / IATA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own facilities maintenance and building operations across office and lab space, including work-order and ticket flow, preventative maintenance, HVAC and BMS, utilities, and emergency power.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the landlord and building-services relationship for day-to-day operations, and hold facilities vendors to scope, quality, and schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in site emergency preparedness and business continuity planning; support drills, incident response, and after-action follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the EHS consultant on lab safety walkthroughs, inspections, and corrective actions, and keep the site audit-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own chemical inventory and SDS management, including the supporting system and the processes around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or co-chair the Safety Committee, and drive safety programs, training compliance, and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational systems behind both functions (ServiceNow request and ticketing, asset and inventory platforms); drive adoption, reporting, and training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain the SOPs, policies, and records that keep both functions consistent and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process improvements, including automation and AI tools, that cut manual effort and improve response time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage service vendors and contracts end-to-end: scope, negotiation support, performance, and renewal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and experience you’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a life sciences, engineering, or related field, or equivalent experience; advanced degree a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in laboratory operations, facilities, or site operations within biotech, pharma, or a research environment, including experience leading a high performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on ownership across both lab and facilities scope, or deep expertise in one with credible working knowledge of the other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of lab EHS, chemical hygiene, hazardous-materials handling, and the regulatory expectations for a research site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with building systems and environmental monitoring, and with alarm response and escalation in a lab environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning an operating budget, with financial tracking and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with operations systems (ticketing such as ServiceNow, asset management, inventory) and with vendor and contract management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment under pressure, with real ownership and follow-through, and the ability to move between strategy and the floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to be on-site role in an active laboratory and office environment, with availability for occasional off-hours response to facility and lab incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
